// Subjects a visitor will ask about that the corpus knowingly does not hold.
//
// Not a list of things nobody wrote about -- the matcher handles those by
// finding nothing. This is for subjects that exist in the world of the project
// and are deliberately absent from the index, where "nothing here matches"
// would be misleading and "not yet" is the truth.
//
// Each key is matched against the visitor's words, case-insensitively, as whole
// words. The reply is a frame: the text here is quoted verbatim.
Absent(
    subjects: {
        // The 1442 card read punch is withheld on purpose: it is the held-out
        // exhibit for the new-resource experiment (plan.md Saga 7, SN01), and
        // the campus will publish it as a dated event. Its wing mentions it in
        // prose, which is exactly why a visitor asks and why the honest answer
        // is "not yet" rather than a route to the wing.
        "1442": "The IBM 1442 card read punch is not an exhibit yet. The 1130 wing mentions it among the machine's peripherals, and it is the next thing due to open there.",
        "card read punch": "The IBM 1442 card read punch is not an exhibit yet. The 1130 wing mentions it among the machine's peripherals, and it is the next thing due to open there.",
        "card reader": "The card reader -- the IBM 1442 -- is not an exhibit yet. The 1130 wing mentions it among the machine's peripherals, and it is the next thing due to open there.",
    },
)
